<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n104806" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρῐάς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">άδος</span>, ἡ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρεῖς</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>the number three, triad,</i> Ion
				Hist.<i><span class="en">
				12
			</span></i> note, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Phd.</u>
				104a
			</span></i>, al.; on its significance in the <i><span class="en">
				Pythag.
			</span></i> philosophy, v.
			<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Cael.</u>
				268a13
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Metaph.</u>
				1081a34
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				b12
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρισσὴν . . ἐτέων
			τριάδα</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γεγονώς</span>), i.
			e. nine years old, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Syria</u>
				5.338
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Sidon</span>); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τ. ἡ
				ἀκατονόμαστος,</span> of the mystical Man from heaven
				(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεόσ—ἄγγελοσ—ἄνθρωπος
			παθητός</span>), Zos.Alch.<i><span class="en">
				p.230
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				B.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ τ.</span>
			<i>group of three days,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τελευτᾷ ἐν τῇ πρώτῃ τ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Thphr.
					<u>Vent.</u>
					49
				</span></i>
			; the <i>third day,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				1.13
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>system of three strophes,</i> Heph.<i><span class="en">
				p.61C.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ ἁγία</span> T. the holy <i>Trinity,
				Cod. Just.</i><i><span class="en">
				1.1.5.2
			</span></i>, etc.</div>
